<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A2.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">WSD with different decay ratios:<span id="A2.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We train a 400M LLaMA (dense) model with 20B tokens of training data and WSD LRSs with the ratios between stable time and decay time of 3:1, 4:1, and 5:1. All WSD LRSs exhibit a final loss similar to that of the Cosine LRS, and the optimal LRS derived from our functional scaling law outperforms all other LRSs by a loss gap of approximately 0.01.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19189v1/wsd_to_0.svg" id="A2.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/179;" width="238" height="179"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A2.F10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison between optimal LRS and WSD with a near-zero final learning rate:<span id="A2.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We train a 100M LLaMA (dense) model with 40B tokens training data and various LRSs with the same <math id="A2.F10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\max}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\max}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, including WSD LRS with <math id="A2.F10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> = <math id="A2.F10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, WSD LRS with <math id="A2.F10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}=10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}=10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math>, cosine LRS with <math id="A2.F10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}=\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}=\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, 8-1-1 LRS with <math id="A2.F10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}=\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}=\frac{1}{10}\eta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, and optimal LRS. The experimental results show that decaying to (near) zero does not result in significant loss reduction.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Intrinsic-time Functional Scaling Law (FSL)). ‣ 4 Functional Scaling Laws ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Preliminaries</h4>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.1 </span>Connections to kernel regression</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we aim to explain the assumptions made in
section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, namely
Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2 (Model Capacity). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 2.3 (Task difficulty). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our setting is highly related to the classical kernel regression. In kernel
regression, we aim to learn a function within a reproducing kernel Hilbert space
(RKHS) from finite data samples. We begin by reviewing the foundational setup of
kernel regression and subsequently show the connections between our assumptions
and the classical ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact topological space. Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability measure on
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> the marginal distribution on <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a continuous PSD kernel
such that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{x}}[K(x,x)]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{x}}[K(x,x)]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
and we denote the corresponding RKHS by <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For some <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{x}:=K(x,\cdot)\in\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{x}:=K(x,\cdot)\in\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, we assume that there exists a function <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that the distribution <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=f^{*}(x)+\epsilon,\quad x\sim\rho_{x}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=f^{*}(x)+\epsilon,\quad x\sim\rho_{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable independent of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\epsilon]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\epsilon]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\epsilon^{2}]=\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\epsilon^{2}]=\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We call <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> the target function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the excess risk as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(f)=\frac{1}{2}\|f-f^{*}\|_{L^{2}_{\rho_{x}}(\mathcal{X})}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{x}}[(f(x)-f^{*}(x))^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(f)=\frac{1}{2}\|f-f^{*}\|_{L^{2}_{\rho_{x}}(\mathcal{X})}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho_{x}}[(f(x)-f^{*}(x))^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Our objective is to minimize the excess risk. The dataset is i.i.d. drawn from
the distribution <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Given a PSD kernel <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
by Mercer’s theorem there exists a nonnegative sequence
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and an orthonormal basis
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}_{\rho}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}_{\rho}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x,x^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}e_{j}(x)e_{j}(x^{\prime})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x,x^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}e_{j}(x)e_{j}(x^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where the series converges absolutely and uniformly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Define the feature functions <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{j}(x)=\lambda_{j}^{\frac{1}{2}}e_{j}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{j}(x)=\lambda_{j}^{\frac{1}{2}}e_{j}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the RHKS <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x,x^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\phi_{j}(x)\phi_{j}(x^{\prime}),\quad\mathcal{H}_{K}=\left\{\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}\phi_{j}:\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}^{2}&lt;\infty\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x,x^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\phi_{j}(x)\phi_{j}(x^{\prime}),\quad\mathcal{H}_{K}=\left\{\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}\phi_{j}:\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}^{2}&lt;\infty\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> being an orthonormal basis of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also we have <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi_{j}(x)^{2}]=\lambda_{j}\mathbb{E}[e_{j}(x)^{2}]=\lambda_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi_{j}(x)^{2}]=\lambda_{j}\mathbb{E}[e_{j}(x)^{2}]=\lambda_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{j}\}_{j=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is still orthogonal in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}_{\rho}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}_{\rho}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The interpolation space <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}=\left\{\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}\phi_{j}:\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\frac{a_{j}^{2}}{\lambda_{j}^{s-1}}&lt;\infty\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}=\left\{\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}a_{j}\phi_{j}:\sum_{j=1}^{\infty}\frac{a_{j}^{2}}{\lambda_{j}^{s-1}}&lt;\infty\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}^{0}=L^{2}_{\rho_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}^{0}=L^{2}_{\rho_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}^{1}=\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}^{1}=\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s_{1}}\subset\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s_{1}}\subset\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}&gt;s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}&gt;s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The source-capacity condition are usually given as</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Capacity condition)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists some <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}=O(j^{-\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}=O(j^{-\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Source condition)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists some <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}(x)\in\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}(x)\in\mathcal{H}_{K}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2 (Model Capacity). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 2.3 (Task difficulty). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>,
the parameter <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> here, therefore
they are the power-law version of the standard source-capacity condition,
which gives the following insights:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A smaller <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the target function <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in a
larger space, hence the learning problem is more difficult.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A smaller <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the RKHS <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is larger,
and in our setting <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the hypothesis space,
meaning that the model capacity is larger.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>The SDE modeling</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our setup, the SGD update can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{k}=\mathbf{v}_{k-1}-\varphi_{k}\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})h-\varphi_{k}h\bm{\xi}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{k}=\mathbf{v}_{k-1}-\varphi_{k}\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})h-\varphi_{k}h\bm{\xi}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\xi}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\xi}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the gradient noise, whose covariance
is <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{B_{k}}\Sigma(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{B_{k}}\Sigma(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore in order to approximate it as an Itô-type SDE,
we assume the noise is Gaussian and write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{k}-\mathbf{v}_{k-1}=-\varphi_{k}\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})h+\varphi_{k}\sqrt{\frac{h}{B_{k}}\Sigma(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})}\sqrt{h}\mathbf{z},\quad\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt><mi>𝐳</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{k}-\mathbf{v}_{k-1}=-\varphi_{k}\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})h+\varphi_{k}\sqrt{\frac{h}{B_{k}}\Sigma(\mathbf{v}_{k-1})}\sqrt{h}\mathbf{z},\quad\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Hence the corresponding SDE (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 The Intrinsic-Time Stochastic Differential Equations ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau}=-\varphi(\tau)\nabla\mathcal{R}(\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\varphi(\tau)\sqrt{\frac{h}{b(\tau)}\Sigma(\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau})}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau}=-\varphi(\tau)\nabla\mathcal{R}(\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\varphi(\tau)\sqrt{\frac{h}{b(\tau)}\Sigma(\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{\tau})}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{\tau}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Brownian
motion, and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are the continuous version of LRS function and
batch-size schedule function, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will derive a Volterra integral equation of the excess
risk from the intrinsic-time SDE.
Recall the intrinsic-time SDE:</p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bm{\nu}_{t}=-\nabla\mathcal{R}(\bm{\nu}_{t})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma(\bm{\nu}_{t})}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bm{\nu}_{t}=-\nabla\mathcal{R}(\bm{\nu}_{t})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma(\bm{\nu}_{t})}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}=\gamma_{\varphi,b}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}=\gamma_{\varphi,b}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, we drop the dependence on <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.3 Online Minibatch SGD ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we have
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\theta^{*})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\theta^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{t}=\mathbf{W}^{\top}\bm{\nu}_{t}-\bm{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{t}=\mathbf{W}^{\top}\bm{\nu}_{t}-\bm{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{u}_{t})=\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{t}\|_{\mathbf{H}}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{u}_{t})=\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{t}\|_{\mathbf{H}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">To obtain the estimate of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider
the intrinsic-time SDE for <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> given by:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}:=\Sigma(\bm{\nu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝛎</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}:=\Sigma(\bm{\nu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Eq. (<a href="#A3.E14" title="In C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\bm{\nu}_{t}-\mathbf{v}^{*})=\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bm{\nu}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{W}^{\top}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma_{t}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝝂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\bm{\nu}_{t}-\mathbf{v}^{*})=\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\bm{\nu}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\mathbf{W}^{\top}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma_{t}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> dimensional standard Brownian motion,
we are going to replace it with an <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> dimensional standard Brownian motion
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to see that the diffusion term <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{\top}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma_{t}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{\top}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\Sigma_{t}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tilde{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same distribution
as <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence the SDE can be written in <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathbf{B}}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathbf{B}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">A key insight for tractability is that the gradient noise exhibits the following anisotropic structure:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our analytic analysis also relies on the noise structure characterized by the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Noise Structure)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2C_{1}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\sigma^{2})\,\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\preceq\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\preceq(2C_{2}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\sigma^{2})\,\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2C_{1}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\sigma^{2})\,\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\preceq\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\preceq(2C_{2}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\sigma^{2})\,\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Noting <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\frac{1}{2}\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})+\frac{1}{2}\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, this lemma means
<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\eqsim\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\eqsim\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v}).</annotation></semantics></math>
That is, the gradient noise scales proportionally with the population risk and aligns with the local curvature. Notably, the noise has two distinct sources: (i) the fit-dependent term <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math>, which arises purely from minibatching and persists even in the absence of label noise;
(ii) the <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> term, which captures the contribution from label noise. This anisotropic structure of SGD noise – scaling with risk and shaped by curvature – has also been observed in prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>, <a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Noting <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})=\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{v}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})-y)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})=\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{v}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})-y)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\bm{\theta}^{*}\right)-\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\bm{\theta}^{*}\right)-\mathbf{W}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})]=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\bm{\theta}^{*}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})]=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{v}-\bm{\theta}^{*}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the covariance matrix of the noise <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\xi}:=\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})-\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝃</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\xi}:=\nabla\ell(\mathbf{z};\mathbf{v})-\nabla\mathcal{R}(\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma(\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma(\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\bm{\xi}\bm{\xi}^{\top}|\mathbf{v}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝃</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\bm{\xi}\bm{\xi}^{\top}|\mathbf{v}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\right)\mathbf{W}^{\top}+\sigma^{2}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\right)\mathbf{W}^{\top}+\sigma^{2}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Noting</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})\bm{\phi}(\mathbf{x})^{\top}\right]-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{H},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">then applying Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 2.1 (Hypercontractivity condition). ‣ 2.1 Teacher–Student Kernel Regression ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\preceq C_{2}\mathbf{W}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top})\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}+\sigma^{2}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}=\left(2C_{2}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{u})+\sigma^{2}\right)\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma(\mathbf{v})\preceq C_{2}\mathbf{W}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top})\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}+\sigma^{2}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}=\left(2C_{2}\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{u})+\sigma^{2}\right)\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step follows from <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top})=\|\mathbf{u}\|_{\mathbf{H}}^{2}=2\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐮𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}\mathbf{u}^{\top})=\|\mathbf{u}\|_{\mathbf{H}}^{2}=2\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v})</annotation></semantics></math>. The lower bound follows the same proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The excess-risk dynamics</span> is then given by the following Volterra integral
equation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the intrinsic-time SDE, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})\cdot\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})\cdot\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{t}:=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{t}:=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}:=\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}:=\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2C_{1}\leqslant c_{\tau}\leqslant 2C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2C_{1}\leqslant c_{\tau}\leqslant 2C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are some constants.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Itô’s formula,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}(e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\mathbf{u}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}(e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\mathbf{u}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\sqrt{\gamma_{t}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{t}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating both sides, we get</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\mathbf{u}_{t}-\mathbf{u}_{0}=\int_{0}^{t}e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\tau}\sqrt{\gamma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}\mathbf{u}_{t}-\mathbf{u}_{0}=\int_{0}^{t}e^{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\tau}\sqrt{\gamma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now write <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{t}=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{t}=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{t}=\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\gamma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{t}=\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\gamma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the integral with respect to <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> always has
zero expectation, therefore we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\mathbb{E}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\mathbb{E}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma E.2. ‣ Appendix E Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Noise Structure). ‣ C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\leqslant(2\mathcal{E}_{\tau}+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\leqslant(2\mathcal{E}_{\tau}+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\geqslant(\mathcal{E}_{\tau}+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)\geqslant(\mathcal{E}_{\tau}+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence there exists some constant <math id="A3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\tau}\in[2C_{1},2C_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\tau}\in[2C_{1},2C_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)=(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\mathrm{tr}\left(\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\Sigma_{\tau}\mathbf{W}}\right)=(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">from which the lemma follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>The <span id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">g</span> Functions</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our analysis will frequently use following family of functions</p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{a}(t)=g_{a}^{(M)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{a}(t)=g_{a}^{(M)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{a}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{a}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\lim_{M\to\infty}g_{a}^{(M)}(t)=\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\lim_{M\to\infty}g_{a}^{(M)}(t)=\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the forgetting kernel and risk functions are special cases:</p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t),\quad e(t)=g_{s}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t),\quad e(t)=g_{s}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{a},\quad g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(a)}{(2t)^{a}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{a},\quad g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(a)}{(2t)^{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof only involves calculating the integral. Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a}(t)\leqslant\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\leqslant\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{1}{a}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a}(t)\leqslant\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\leqslant\int_{0}^{1}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{1}{a},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{(2t)^{a}}\int_{0}^{\infty}u^{a-1}e^{-u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{\Gamma(a)}{(2t)^{a}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{(2t)^{a}}\int_{0}^{\infty}u^{a-1}e^{-u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{\Gamma(a)}{(2t)^{a}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\Omega(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\Omega(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{a}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{a}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(2t)^{a}}\int_{tM^{-\beta}}^{t}u^{a-1}e^{-u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{(2t)^{a}}\int_{tM^{-\beta}}^{t}u^{a-1}e^{-u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The integral part is a partial gamma function, hence when
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tM^{-\beta}\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tM^{-\beta}\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{a}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}u^{a-1}e^{-2u\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{0}^{t}u^{a-1}e^{-2u\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2ut}}{2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2ut}}{2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-M^{-(a-1)\beta}}{2(a-1)}-\frac{1}{2}g_{a-1}(t)\lesssim 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-M^{-(a-1)\beta}}{2(a-1)}-\frac{1}{2}g_{a-1}(t)\lesssim 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, when <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\Omega(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\Omega(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{a-1}(t)&lt;\frac{1}{(a-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{a-1}(t)&lt;\frac{1}{(a-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
combining with <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\geqslant 0,t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\geqslant 0,t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{a\wedge b}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{a\wedge b}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\wedge b:=\min\{a,b\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\wedge b:=\min\{a,b\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we can assume <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geqslant b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geqslant b</annotation></semantics></math>. By Hölder’s Inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(\tau(t-\tau))^{b}}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(\tau(t-\tau))^{b}}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(\tau(t-\tau))^{b}}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(\tau(t-\tau))^{b}}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b-1}}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\left(\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}+\frac{1}{\tau^{b}(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b-1}}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\left(\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}+\frac{1}{\tau^{b}(t-\tau)^{a-b}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b}}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{\tau^{a}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b}}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{\tau^{a}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b}a}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{b}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2^{b}a}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{b}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.9</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,M</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\geqslant 0,t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\geqslant 0,t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim g_{a\wedge b}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim g_{a\wedge b}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\wedge b:=\min\{a,b\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\wedge b:=\min\{a,b\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we can assume <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geqslant b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geqslant b</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, using Fubini’s theorem gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}v^{b-1}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}e^{-2v\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}v^{b-1}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}e^{-2v\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}v^{b-1}\frac{e^{-2vt}-e^{-2ut}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}v^{b-1}\frac{e^{-2vt}-e^{-2ut}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}v^{b-1}e^{-2vt}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}v^{b-1}e^{-2vt}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}v</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower bound:<span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  Let <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{1}=\frac{\log 2}{2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{1}=\frac{\log 2}{2t}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{v-\epsilon}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\int_{v+\epsilon}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{v-\epsilon}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\int_{v+\epsilon}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that when <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u-v|\geqslant\frac{\log 2}{2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u-v|\geqslant\frac{\log 2}{2t}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\geqslant\frac{1}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\geqslant\frac{1}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">and we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{4}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{v-\epsilon}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\int_{v+\epsilon}^{1}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)=\frac{1}{4}\left(1-M^{-a\beta}-\int_{v-\epsilon}^{v+\epsilon}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{4}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{v-\epsilon}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\int_{v+\epsilon}^{1}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)=\frac{1}{4}\left(1-M^{-a\beta}-\int_{v-\epsilon}^{v+\epsilon}u^{a-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{a-1}\leqslant 1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{a-1}\leqslant 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">and thus</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{4}\left(1-M^{-a\beta}-\frac{\log 2}{t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{4}\left(1-M^{-a\beta}-\frac{\log 2}{t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,t=\Omega(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,t=\Omega(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-a\beta}&lt;\frac{1}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-a\beta}&lt;\frac{1}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\log 2}{t}&lt;\frac{1}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\log 2}{t}&lt;\frac{1}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining them together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{8}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{a-1}\frac{1-e^{-2(u-v)t}}{2(u-v)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{8},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\geqslant\frac{1}{8}g_{M}(a\wedge b,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\geqslant\frac{1}{8}g_{M}(a\wedge b,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Upper bound:<span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  By lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a></span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}{2^{a+b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}{2^{a+b}}\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We observe that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{a}\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{a}\frac{1}{t^{b}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{a}\int_{t-1}^{t}g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{a}\frac{1}{t^{b}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">and for the same reason</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{b}\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{t^{a}}\leqslant\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{t^{b}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{b}\int_{0}^{1}g_{a}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{t^{a}}\leqslant\frac{1}{b}\frac{1}{t^{b}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, by the Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma C.8. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{a\wedge b}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{1}^{t-1}\frac{1}{(t-\tau)^{a}}\frac{1}{\tau^{b}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\frac{8}{t^{a\wedge b}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combine them together we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\left(\frac{1}{a}+\frac{1}{b}+8\right)\frac{1}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{10}{t^{b}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\left(\frac{1}{a}+\frac{1}{b}+8\right)\frac{1}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{10}{t^{b}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-\beta}t&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-\beta}t&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{b}(t)=\frac{1}{t^{b}}\int_{M^{-\beta}t}^{t}u^{b-1}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t_{0}}u^{b-1}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{C_{1}}{t^{b}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{b}(t)=\frac{1}{t^{b}}\int_{M^{-\beta}t}^{t}u^{b-1}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\geqslant\frac{1}{t^{b}}\int_{1}^{t_{0}}u^{b-1}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{C_{1}}{t^{b}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">So we can give the upper bound</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant 10\frac{1}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{10}{C_{1}}g_{a\wedge b}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{a}(t-\tau)g_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant 10\frac{1}{t^{b}}\leqslant\frac{10}{C_{1}}g_{a\wedge b}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">By combining the lower and upper bounds, we complete the proof of the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{a}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{a}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the following lemma follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a> immediately
by taking <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.10</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}G_{a}(t-\tau)G_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim G_{a\wedge b}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}G_{a}(t-\tau)G_{b}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim G_{a\wedge b}(t).</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>The Case of Top-<span id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">M</span> Features</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we prove the functional scaling law for the case of top-<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>
features. Recall the choice of top-<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> features, where we choose <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}=[\mathbf{I}_{M},\bm{0}_{M\times(N-M)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}=[\mathbf{I}_{M},\bm{0}_{M\times(N-M)}]</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case we can
simplify the SDE and the expression of the <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we will estimate
each term of the Volterra equation to complete the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.11</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The intrinsic-time SDE of top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> case)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the projector <math id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}=[\mathbf{I}_{M},\bm{0}_{M\times(N-M)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}=[\mathbf{I}_{M},\bm{0}_{M\times(N-M)}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{H}_{0:M}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{H}_{0:M}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{H}_{0:M}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{H}_{0:M}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{0:M}=\operatorname{diag}\{\underbrace{\lambda_{1},...,\lambda_{M}}_{M},\underbrace{0,...,0}_{N-M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>diag</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>M</mi></munder><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{0:M}=\operatorname{diag}\{\underbrace{\lambda_{1},...,\lambda_{M}}_{M},\underbrace{0,...,0}_{N-M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that from Eq. (<a href="#A3.E15" title="In Lemma C.3. ‣ C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}=\operatorname{diag}\{\underbrace{1,...,1}_{M},\underbrace{0,...,0}_{N-M}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>M</mi></munder><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}=\operatorname{diag}\{\underbrace{1,...,1}_{M},\underbrace{0,...,0}_{N-M}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}=\mathbf{H}_{0:M},\qquad\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{H}_{0:M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}=\mathbf{H}_{0:M},\qquad\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{H}_{0:M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combine these results and we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{H}_{0:M}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{H}_{0:M}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{u}_{t}=-\mathbf{H}_{0:M}\mathbf{u}_{t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\gamma_{t}(c_{t}\mathcal{E}_{t}+\sigma^{2})}\sqrt{\mathbf{H}_{0:M}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We have the following recursion for <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.12</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Volterra equation of the top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> case)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\left(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\left(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is mainly based on the Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma C.11 (The intrinsic-time SDE of top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.11</span></a>. Similarly, we decompose the SDE into its individual components, solve the resulting equations. By addressing each component individually, we can derive precise solutions and expectations for <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{(j)})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{(j)})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leqslant j\leqslant M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leqslant j\leqslant M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{(j)})^{2}]=e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}+\lambda_{j}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{u}_{t}^{(j)})^{2}]=e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}+\lambda_{j}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We then calculate the risk:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}+\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v}_{\tau})]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}+\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v}_{\tau})]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}}_{I_{1}}+\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v}_{\tau})])\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau}_{I_{2}}+\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau}_{I_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}}_{I_{1}}+\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{v}_{\tau})])\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau}_{I_{2}}+\underbrace{\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}(\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau}_{I_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}}_{I_{4}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}\lambda_{j}(\mathbf{v}_{0}^{(j)})^{2}}_{I_{4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We next shall bound the four terms separately.</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> term.</span>
We can substitute <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate the sum by integral</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\sum_{j=1}^{M}j^{-s\beta-1}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}x^{-s\beta-1}e^{-2x^{-\beta}t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=\frac{1}{\beta}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{s-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim g_{s}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\sum_{j=1}^{M}j^{-s\beta-1}e^{-2\lambda_{j}t}\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}x^{-s\beta-1}e^{-2x^{-\beta}t}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=\frac{1}{\beta}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{s-1}e^{-2ut}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim g_{s}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> term.</span>
Similarly, we substitute <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate the sum by integral</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex113.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\int_{1}^{M}x^{2\beta}(e^{-2x^{-\beta}(t-\tau)})dx\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\int_{1}^{M}x^{2\beta}(e^{-2x^{-\beta}(t-\tau)})dx\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}du\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}du\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> term.</span>
Similarly, we substitude <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate the sum by integral</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\right)\eqsim\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\int_{1}^{M}x^{2\beta}(e^{-2x^{-\beta}(t-\tau)})dx\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{M}\lambda_{j}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{j}(t-\tau)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\right)\eqsim\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\int_{1}^{M}x^{2\beta}(e^{-2x^{-\beta}(t-\tau)})dx\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}du\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\sigma^{2}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{\tau}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(t-\tau)}du\right)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\sigma^{2}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> term.</span>
By approximating the sum with the integral, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{4}=\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}j^{-1-s\beta}\eqsim\int_{M}^{\infty}x^{-1-s\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{4}=\sum_{j=M+1}^{\infty}j^{-1-s\beta}\eqsim\int_{M}^{\infty}x^{-1-s\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining them together completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.13</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Functional Scaling Law of the top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> case)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\max}:=\sup_{t}\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\max}:=\sup_{t}\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small. Then, for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s\in(0,2-1/\beta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,2-1/\beta]</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\left(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(\tau)\right)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\left(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(\tau)\right)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The case of <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\geqslant t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩾</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\geqslant t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> The condition of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a> holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma C.12 (Volterra equation of the top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">First we define <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then we calculate the last term. By Fubini’s theorem,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathcal{K}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathcal{K}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C\gamma_{\max}B(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C\gamma_{\max}B(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>.
Therefore, we get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{1}{1-C\gamma_{\max}}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{1}{1-C\gamma_{\max}}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex127.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gamma_{\max}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gamma_{\max}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t):=\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,\quad q(t):=\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t):=\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,\quad q(t):=\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Noting <math id="A3.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex129.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+(\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta})p(t)+q(t)+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+(\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta})p(t)+q(t)+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The last term can be bounded as follows</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leqslant}}C\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\mathcal{K}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=C\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}p(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leqslant}}C\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\mathcal{K}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=C\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}p(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> uses Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>.
Suppose <math id="A3.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gamma_{\max}&lt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gamma_{\max}&lt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+(\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta})p(t)+q(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+(\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta})p(t)+q(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A3.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> to be sufficiently small such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)\leqslant\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\gamma_{\max}\frac{\beta}{2(\beta-1)}&lt;\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)\leqslant\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}g_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\gamma_{\max}\frac{\beta}{2(\beta-1)}&lt;\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}p(t)+q(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}p(t)+q(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(\tau))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{s}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(\tau))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The case of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\leqslant t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\leqslant t</annotation></semantics></math>:</h6>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The condition of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a> does not hold. In this case,
we first analyze the left-hand side of the equation. The key idea is to make a small modification to <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and use similar methods to prove the result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A3.Ex119" title="In Proof. ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A3.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau=:\tilde{B}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau=:\tilde{B}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We next proceed to estimate <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> in an analogous manner.</p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{B}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{B}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Then we calculate the last term. By Fubini’s theorem,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex144.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}c_{r}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{r}]\gamma_{r}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C\gamma_{\max}\tilde{B}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C\gamma_{\max}\tilde{B}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality is by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma C.10. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>.
Therefore, we get</p>
<table id="A3.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{1-C\gamma_{\max}}\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}(t)\leqslant\frac{1}{1-C\gamma_{\max}}\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}(t)\geqslant\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩾</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}(t)\geqslant\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gamma_{\max}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gamma_{\max}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Next we bound the last term</p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t}\gamma_{r}\int_{r}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau-r)\gamma_{\max}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-r)\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality is again by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma C.10. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Also we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex156.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}\frac{1-e^{-2ut}}{2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}\frac{1-e^{-2ut}}{2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}\frac{1}{2u}\eqsim 1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}\frac{1}{2u}\eqsim 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since we assumed that <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, we also have <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly</p>
<table id="A3.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}(G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)-\mathcal{K}(\tau))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{M^{-\beta}}u^{-1/\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim\gamma_{\max}M^{1-\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>≲</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></msubsup><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>≂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}(G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)-\mathcal{K}(\tau))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max}\int_{0}^{M^{-\beta}}u^{-1/\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim\gamma_{\max}M^{1-\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which implies <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, continuing the computation of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,
since</p>
<table id="A3.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&lt;t\implies M^{-2\beta+1}\geqslant t^{-(2-\frac{1}{\beta})}\gtrsim G_{2-1/\beta}(t)\geqslant\mathcal{K}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⩾</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&lt;t\implies M^{-2\beta+1}\geqslant t^{-(2-\frac{1}{\beta})}\gtrsim G_{2-1/\beta}(t)\geqslant\mathcal{K}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">we have <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-\beta}+G_{2-1/\beta}(t)\eqsim M^{-\beta}+\mathcal{K}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-\beta}+G_{2-1/\beta}(t)\eqsim M^{-\beta}+\mathcal{K}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence similar to the proof in the first case, let</p>
<table id="A3.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t):=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max},\quad q(t):=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t):=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max},\quad q(t):=\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}g_{s}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\max\{1,M^{-s\beta+\beta}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}g_{s}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\max\{1,M^{-s\beta+\beta}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, by <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 2-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 2-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(M^{-s\beta},M^{-\beta})\geqslant M^{-2\beta+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(M^{-s\beta},M^{-\beta})\geqslant M^{-2\beta+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(t)+M^{-s\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(t)+M^{-s\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex162.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}(G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)+M^{-2\beta+1})g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}(G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)+M^{-2\beta+1})g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}(g_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)+M^{-2\beta+1})g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}(g_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)+M^{-2\beta+1})g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)g_{s}(\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore by <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(\tau)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau\lesssim\gamma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{B}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{B}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex165.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{t}G_{2-1/\beta}(t-\tau)\,c_{\tau}\gamma_{\tau}\left(g_{s}(\tau)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{\tau}\mathcal{K}(\tau-r)c_{r}\gamma_{r}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim q(t)+M^{-s\beta}p(t)+\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim q(t)+M^{-s\beta}p(t)+\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}p(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim q(t)+\gamma_{\max}M^{-s\beta}+\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim q(t)+\gamma_{\max}M^{-s\beta}+\gamma_{\max}\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Substituting this into the expression of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma C.12 (Volterra equation of the top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>), note that <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(t)=g_{2-1/\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex168.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim g_{s}(t)+\tilde{B}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim g_{s}(t)+\tilde{B}(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim g_{s}(t)+q(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim g_{s}(t)+q(t)+M^{-s\beta}+\sigma^{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(t))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(t))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, clearly <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\gtrsim g_{s}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\gtrsim g_{s}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, thus by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma C.12 (Volterra equation of the top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex171.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}])\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}])\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gtrsim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(t))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gtrsim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)(\sigma^{2}+g_{s}(t))\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.14</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\max}:=\sup_{t}\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\max}:=\sup_{t}\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim G_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\left(\sigma^{2}+G_{s}(\tau)\right)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim G_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\left(\sigma^{2}+G_{s}(\tau)\right)\gamma_{\tau}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the case <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof of Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition C.13 (Functional Scaling Law of the top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>,
the result follows.
Note that in the case <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, we don’t
need the condition of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 2-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 2-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>The Case of Random Features</h4>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we prove Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Intrinsic-time Functional Scaling Law (FSL)). ‣ 4 Functional Scaling Laws ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> for the case of random features.
The proof proceed similarly as the top-<math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> case. First we introduce some
concentration properties of the random martix <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> from
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, then we estimate the upper and lower bound of each term
of the Volterra equation in Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5. ‣ C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.5.1 </span>Concentration Inequalities</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we derived the following recursive equation in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E16" title="In Proposition C.5. ‣ C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A3.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\mathbb{E}\mathcal{E}_{t}=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})\cdot\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathbb{E}\mathcal{E}_{t}=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}+\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})\cdot\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{t}=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{t}=e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}=(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}=(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first introduce the following notation:
for integers <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leqslant a&lt;b\leqslant N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leqslant a&lt;b\leqslant N</annotation></semantics></math> (we allow <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, in this case we regard it as
the same as <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=N</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A3.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\quad\mathbf{H}_{a:b}=\operatorname{diag}\{\lambda_{a+1},\dots,\lambda_{b}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{(b-a)\times(b-a)},\quad\mathbf{u}_{a:b}=((\mathbf{u})_{a+1},\dots,(\mathbf{u})_{b})\in\mathbb{R}^{b-a}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>diag</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad\mathbf{H}_{a:b}=\operatorname{diag}\{\lambda_{a+1},\dots,\lambda_{b}\}\in\mathbb{R}^{(b-a)\times(b-a)},\quad\mathbf{u}_{a:b}=((\mathbf{u})_{a+1},\dots,(\mathbf{u})_{b})\in\mathbb{R}^{b-a},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">while</p>
<table id="A3.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{a:b}=[\mathbf{W}_{a+1},\dots,\mathbf{W}_{b}]\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times(b-a)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{a:b}=[\mathbf{W}_{a+1},\dots,\mathbf{W}_{b}]\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times(b-a)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">is the <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th to <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>-th columns of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To understand this equation with random projection matrix <math id="A3.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we leverage the following concentration results developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.15</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma G.4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist <math id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent constants <math id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c_{1}&lt;c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c_{1}&lt;c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that it holds with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}j^{-\beta}\leqslant\mu_{j}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})\leqslant c_{2}j^{-\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}j^{-\beta}\leqslant\mu_{j}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})\leqslant c_{2}j^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.16</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma G.5 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists some <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> such that
for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the ratio between the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{M}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{M}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-th
and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>-th eigenvalue</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}\leqslant c" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}\leqslant c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.5.2 </span>Upper and Lower Bounds</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}_{j}=\mu_{j}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}_{j}=\mu_{j}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.17</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})=\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}\eqsim\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})=\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}\eqsim\mathcal{K}(t-\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can compute that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{S}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex180.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t-\tau}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t-\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-(t-\tau))^{a+b}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{a}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})^{b}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-(t-\tau))^{a+b}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{a}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})^{b}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\cdot\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b+1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\cdot\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b+1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\cdot(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b+2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left(\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\cdot(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b+2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{a+b+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t+\tau)^{a+b}\sum_{j=1}^{M}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{a+b+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma C.15 (Lemma G.4 in []). ‣ C.5.1 Concentration Inequalities ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}_{j}\eqsim\lambda_{j}\eqsim j^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}_{j}\eqsim\lambda_{j}\eqsim j^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the summation can be estimated by
the integral</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)x^{-\beta}}x^{-2\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}e^{-2(t-\tau)u}u^{2-\frac{1}{\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)\hat{\lambda}_{j}}\hat{\lambda}_{j}^{2}\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}e^{-2(t-\tau)x^{-\beta}}x^{-2\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}e^{-2(t-\tau)u}u^{2-\frac{1}{\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\mathcal{K}(t-\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last but second equality is a change of variable <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=x^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=x^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> in the integral.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the first term in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E16" title="In Proposition C.5. ‣ C.2 Analysis of the Intrinsic-time SDE ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), following
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.18</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\lesssim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\lesssim M^{-s\beta}+g_{s}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{a}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W})^{a}\mathbf{H}(\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})^{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a,b=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{t}=P_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{t}=P_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> being the power series</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(x)=\sum_{a+b\geqslant 0}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}x^{a+b+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(x)=\sum_{a+b\geqslant 0}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}x^{a+b+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that when <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(x)=xe^{-2tx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(x)=xe^{-2tx}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence the eigenvalues of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})\mathbf{u}_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}=\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H})\mathbf{u}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">for any positive integer <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant\frac{M}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant\frac{M}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
note that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}+\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}+\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\leqslant 2(T_{1}+T_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\leqslant 2(T_{1}+T_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k})\mathbf{u}_{0:k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k})\mathbf{u}_{0:k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem21" title="Lemma C.21. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>, we can derive an upper bound.
Since <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{1}+T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{1}+T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{1}{t}\lVert\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\rVert^{2}_{2}+\lVert\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\rVert_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{1}{t}\lVert\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\rVert^{2}_{2}+\lVert\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\rVert_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{1}{t}\sum_{j=1}^{k}j^{-1-s(\beta-1)}+\sum_{j=k+1}^{N}j^{-1-s\beta}\eqsim\frac{k^{-s(\beta-1)}}{t}+k^{-s\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{1}{t}\sum_{j=1}^{k}j^{-1-s(\beta-1)}+\sum_{j=k+1}^{N}j^{-1-s\beta}\eqsim\frac{k^{-s(\beta-1)}}{t}+k^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By setting <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\min\{t^{1/\beta},\frac{M}{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\min\{t^{1/\beta},\frac{M}{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\lesssim\max\{t^{-s},M^{-s\beta}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\lesssim\max\{t^{-s},M^{-s\beta}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now when <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{s}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{s}(t)\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>,
the conclusion follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.19</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex199" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\gtrsim\max\{g_{s}(t),M^{-s\beta}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\gtrsim\max\{g_{s}(t),M^{-s\beta}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following the proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem18" title="Lemma C.18. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\cdot\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{tr}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\cdot\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu_{M-i+1}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\right)\cdot\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu_{M-i+1}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\right)\cdot\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality is by Von Neumann’s trace inequality.
Note that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{t}=P_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{t}=P_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>, we then get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu_{i}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{2}\mathbf{M}_{t}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu_{i}\left((\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{2}\mathbf{M}_{t}^{-1}\right)^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}=\mathbf{v}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}=\mathbf{v}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Assumption
<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2 (Model Capacity). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 2.3 (Task difficulty). ‣ 2.2 The Model Capacity and Task Difficulty ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex205"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{u}_{0}\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex206"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{1+s+1/\beta}\mathbf{W}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{-1}\mu_{i}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{1+s+1/\beta}\mathbf{W}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex207"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gtrsim\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{s+1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gtrsim\sum_{i=1}^{M}e^{-2t\hat{\lambda}_{i}}\hat{\lambda}_{i}^{s+1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}e^{-2tx^{-\beta}}x^{-1-s\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{1}^{M}e^{-2tx^{-\beta}}x^{-1-s\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex209"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}e^{-2tu}u^{s-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=g_{s}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}e^{-2tu}u^{s-1}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=g_{s}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma C.15 (Lemma G.4 in []). ‣ C.5.1 Concentration Inequalities ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, we prove the lower bound on <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. First, we claim that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex210" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\geqslant\|(\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\geqslant\|(\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which will be proved in the Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem20" title="Lemma C.20. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.20</span></a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex211.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\textbf{I}_{k}-\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}-&amp;-\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\\
-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}&amp;\textbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\textbf{I}_{k}-\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}-&amp;-\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\\
-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}&amp;\textbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=:\begin{pmatrix}\mathbf{X}&amp;\mathbf{Y}\\
\mathbf{Y}^{\top}&amp;\mathbf{Z}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝐗</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>𝐘</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mi>𝐙</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=:\begin{pmatrix}\mathbf{X}&amp;\mathbf{Y}\\
\mathbf{Y}^{\top}&amp;\mathbf{Z}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\|(\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\|(\textbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex214"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\right\rangle+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\right\rangle+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex215"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+2\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{X}\mathbf{Y}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Z},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐗𝐘</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐘𝐙</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{u}_{0}}\left\langle\mathbf{X}\mathbf{Y}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Z},\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{1/2}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\mathbf{u}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex216"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})\mathbf{H}_{0:k})+\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y})\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})\mathbf{H}_{0:k})+\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y})\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can calculate that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{Z}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex218" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top}=\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top}=\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{k}=\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{k}=\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">And then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex219"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})\mathbf{H}_{0:k})+\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y})\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{X}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{Y}^{\top})\mathbf{H}_{0:k})+\operatorname{Tr}((\mathbf{Z}^{2}+\mathbf{Y}^{\top}\mathbf{Y})\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex220"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\right)+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1/2}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\right)+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex221"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\right)+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\left[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\right]^{-1}\right)+\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex222"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}):=T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{Z}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}):=T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can then simplify <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex223"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex223.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\left[\textbf{I}_{M-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\left[\textbf{I}_{M-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\left[\textbf{I}_{M-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right]\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\operatorname{Tr}\left(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\left[\textbf{I}_{M-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right]\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\succeq A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⪰</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\succeq A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex225"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex225.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{N-k}\mu_{i}\left(\textbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right)\cdot\mu_{N+1-k-i}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{N-k}\mu_{i}\left(\textbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\right)\cdot\mu_{N+1-k-i}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{N-k}\mu_{i}(\mathbf{M})\cdot\mu_{N+1-k-i}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})\geqslant\sum_{i=k+M}^{N}\lambda_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐌</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\sum_{i=1}^{N-k}\mu_{i}(\mathbf{M})\cdot\mu_{N+1-k-i}(\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty})\geqslant\sum_{i=k+M}^{N}\lambda_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second line follows from <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\succeq A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⪰</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\succeq A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the third line follows from Von-Neuman’s Inequality. Since <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a projection matrix such that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}^{2}=\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}^{2}=\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{M})=N-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Tr}(\mathbf{I}_{N-k}-\mathbf{M})=N-k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvalues <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-k-M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-k-M</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvalues <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> be zero and substitute <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\eqsim i^{-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\eqsim i^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> into the expression above, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex227" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=M}^{N}\lambda_{i}\geqslant cM^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=M}^{N}\lambda_{i}\geqslant cM^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.20</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex228" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\geqslant\|(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{0}^{\top}\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\mathbf{u}_{0}\geqslant\|(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{u}_{0}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of positive semi-definite, we only need to prove that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex229" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\succeq\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})^{2}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}\succeq\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})^{2}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{A}^{\top}_{t}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}t}\mathbf{H}e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}t}\mathbf{H}e^{-\mathbf{W}^{\top}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\left(\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\right)\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\left(\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\right)\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive definite matrix, and now we only need to prove</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex233" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\succeq(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\succeq(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}\mathbf{W}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. After simplification, we only need to prove that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}\succeq\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}\succeq\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that, by the definition of matrix exponential, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex235"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex236"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}+\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\left(\sum_{a+b\geqslant 0}\frac{2^{a+b}}{(a+b)!}(-t)^{a+b}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b}\right)\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}+\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\left(\sum_{a+b\geqslant 0}\frac{2^{a+b}}{(a+b)!}(-t)^{a+b}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b}\right)\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex237"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}+\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}\mathbf{P}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}+\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}\mathbf{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that the matrix <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{\top}\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{\top}\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}</annotation></semantics></math> are both positive semi-definite, we have <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}e^{-2\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top}t}\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semi-definite. As a result,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}\succeq\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}+\sum_{a+b\geqslant 1}\frac{1}{a!b!}(-t)^{a+b}\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{a+b-1}\mathbf{P}\succeq\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{P}^{\top}(\mathbf{P}\mathbf{P}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{P}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p14.7.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.21</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With probability <math id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex239" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{1}\leqslant c\frac{\lVert\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\rVert_{2}^{2}}{t}\left(\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top})}\right)^{2},\quad T_{2}\leqslant\lVert\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\rVert_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>c</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}\leqslant c\frac{\lVert\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\rVert_{2}^{2}}{t}\left(\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top})}\right)^{2},\quad T_{2}\leqslant\lVert\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}\rVert_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is some constant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we prove that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex240" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\leqslant\frac{c}{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\leqslant\frac{c}{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the eigenvalues of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})=\frac{f(2t\hat{\lambda}_{j})}{2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})=\frac{f(2t\hat{\lambda}_{j})}{2t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{0})=x_{0}e^{-x_{0}}\leqslant\frac{1}{e}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{0})=x_{0}e^{-x_{0}}\leqslant\frac{1}{e}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">So we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\leqslant\max_{1\leqslant j\leqslant M}P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})\leqslant\frac{1}{2et}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\leqslant\max_{1\leqslant j\leqslant M}P_{t}(\hat{\lambda}_{j})\leqslant\frac{1}{2et}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex243"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex243.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{M}_{t}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex244"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{M}_{t}\|_{2}\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{c}{t}\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{c}{t}\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{0:k}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">We only need to show</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}\leqslant c\left(\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">⩽</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\|_{2}\leqslant c\left(\frac{\mu_{\frac{M}{2}}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}{\mu_{M}(\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">We denote <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{k}=\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{k}=\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}=\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}+\mathbf{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top}=\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}+\mathbf{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex247"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex247.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}-\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}-\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex248"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}-\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}-\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second line uses Woodbury’s identity. Since</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\succeq\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\succeq\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}\leqslant\|[\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}\leqslant\|[\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex253.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\cdot\|[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\cdot\|[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\cdot\|[\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\cdot\|[\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}}{\mu_{\min}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}\cdot\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}}{\mu_{\min}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.7.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant\frac{M}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant\frac{M}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\leqslant c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">⩽</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\|_{2}\leqslant c</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">We may write <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝒔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{i}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{k}/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{i}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{k}/N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\lambda}_{i})_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\lambda}_{i})_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are eigenvalues of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in non-increasing order.
Therefore, for <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant M/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant M/3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex256" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\sum_{i=1}^{M/2}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M/2}}\sum_{i=1}^{M/2}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\frac{c\mathbf{I}_{k}}{\hat{\lambda}_{M/2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⪰</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\sum_{i=1}^{M/2}\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M-i}}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\frac{1}{\hat{\lambda}_{M/2}}\sum_{i=1}^{M/2}\bm{s}_{i}\bm{s}_{i}^{\top}\succeq\frac{c\mathbf{I}_{k}}{\hat{\lambda}_{M/2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where in the last inequality we again use the concentration properties of Gaussian covariance matrices (see e.g., Theorem 6.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>).</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}[\mathbf{H}_{0:k}^{-1}+\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}]^{-1}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex257.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}}{\mu_{\min}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\|\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\|_{2}}{\mu_{\min}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{0:k})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\mu_{N/2}(\mathbf{A}_{k})}{\mu_{N}(\mathbf{A}_{k})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\mu_{N/2}(\mathbf{A}_{k})}{\mu_{N}(\mathbf{A}_{k})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we focus on <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, by definition of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex259.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}{}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1/2}\exp(-2t\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}{}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1/2}\exp(-2t\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}{}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}{}^{\top}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|\cdot\|\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}\|^{2}_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|\cdot\|\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}\|^{2}_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}\|^{2}_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{u}_{k:\infty}^{*}\|^{2}_{\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line follows from</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex263.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖𝐇𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mathbf{W}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{W}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}+\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}(\mathbf{W}_{0:k}\mathbf{H}_{0:k}\mathbf{W}_{0:k}^{\top}+\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top})^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}\leqslant 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">⩽</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\|\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}^{\top}\mathbf{A}_{k}^{-1}\mathbf{W}_{k:\infty}\mathbf{H}_{k:\infty}^{1/2}\|_{2}\leqslant 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem17" title="Lemma C.17. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>, <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem18" title="Lemma C.18. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>
and <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem19" title="Lemma C.19. ‣ C.5.2 Upper and Lower Bounds ‣ C.5 The Case of Random Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.19</span></a>, we get
with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{t}]\eqsim g_{s}(t)+\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-\tau)\gamma_{\tau}(c_{\tau}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{\tau}]+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS2.p21.2" class="ltx_p">which is of the same form as in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma C.12 (Volterra equation of the top-𝑀 case). ‣ C.4 The Case of Top-M Features ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>.
From here following the same proof as before, we get the
functional scaling laws for random projection matrices.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S5" title="5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proofs for Constant LRS</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we prove Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Scaling law for constant LRS). ‣ 5.1 Constant LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> and present the data-optimal scaling strategy, as well as some results related to the compute-optimal allocation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Scaling law for constant LRS). ‣ 5.1 Constant LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When the learning rate <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(k)\equiv\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(k)\equiv\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are
constants, for the top-<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> selection of the projection matrix
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> or for the random case with probability at least
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex266" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+\frac{\eta}{B}\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+\frac{\eta}{B}\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By our main Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Intrinsic-time Functional Scaling Law (FSL)). ‣ 4 Functional Scaling Laws ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, when the learning rate <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(k)\equiv\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(k)\equiv\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:=\frac{\eta}{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:=\frac{\eta}{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex267" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim(t)^{-s}+\gamma\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-r)(e(r)+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim(t)^{-s}+\gamma\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{K}(t-r)(e(r)+\sigma^{2})\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\tau+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 The g Functions ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>, note that when <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math> we have
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}\gtrsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}\gtrsim e(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≳</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}\gtrsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}\gtrsim e(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,
therefore</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex268" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}+\frac{\gamma}{t^{s}}+\gamma\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\frac{1}{t^{s}}+\frac{\gamma}{t^{s}}+\gamma\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.Ex269" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{t^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{t^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we may write it as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex270" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{t^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{t^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\eta K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\eta K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{\eta}{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{\eta}{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex271" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+\frac{\eta}{B}\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{K}]-\frac{\sigma^{2}}{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+\frac{\eta}{B}\sigma^{2}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a total data size of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal strategy for
minimizing the final population risk, in terms of the effective learning
rate <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and model size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{1}{(1+s)\beta}},\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{1}{(1+s)\beta}},\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex272" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By weighted AM-GM inequality, we have that when <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized, it must hold that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex273" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\sigma^{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\sigma^{2}\eqsim\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex274" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into the error expression yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex275" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">To balance the two terms and achieve the optimal rate, we require</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex276" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{1}{(1+s)\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{1}{(1+s)\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, the optimal loss rate becomes</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex277" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s}{s+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Next we consider the compute optimal strategy for constant learning rates.
We define the compute <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=MKB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=MKB</annotation></semantics></math> to be the product of the model size,
training steps and batch size.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a total compute budget of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal strategy for
minimizing the final population risk, in terms of the effective learning
rate <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, model size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, and data size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=BK" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=BK</annotation></semantics></math>, is:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex278" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex278.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta+s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta+s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex279" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex279.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{1}{(\eta K)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">substituting <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\frac{C}{MB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\frac{C}{MB}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex280" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex280.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{K}]\eqsim\gamma\sigma^{2}+\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">By weighted AM-GM inequality, we have that when <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is
minimized, it must hold that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex281" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex281.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\sigma^{2}\eqsim\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}},\quad\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\sigma^{2}\eqsim\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}},\quad\frac{M^{s}}{(C\gamma)^{s}}\eqsim M^{-s\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">which gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex282" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex282.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Now we can further compute <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=BK=CM^{-1}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta+s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=BK=CM^{-1}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta+s\beta}{1+\beta+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof for The Exponential-Decay LRS</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the LRS given by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex283" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex283.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\tau)=ae^{-\lambda\tau},\text{ with }\varphi(K)=b," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\tau)=ae^{-\lambda\tau},\text{ with }\varphi(K)=b,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\log(a/b)/K=:1/\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\log(a/b)/K=:1/\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the intrinsic-time transform is given by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex284" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex284.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\tau)=\int_{0}^{\tau}\varphi(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=\frac{a}{\lambda}\left(1-e^{-\lambda\tau}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\tau)=\int_{0}^{\tau}\varphi(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=\frac{a}{\lambda}\left(1-e^{-\lambda\tau}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total intrinsic time is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex285" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex285.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(K)=\frac{a}{\lambda}(1-e^{-\lambda K})=\frac{K}{\log(a/b)}(a-b)=:\bar{K}(a-b)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(K)=\frac{a}{\lambda}(1-e^{-\lambda K})=\frac{K}{\log(a/b)}(a-b)=:\bar{K}(a-b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, we shall write <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=T(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=T(K)</annotation></semantics></math> in what follows.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The LRS-adjusted function in intrinsic time is given by</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<table id="A4.Ex286" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex286.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\varphi}(t)=\varphi(T^{-1}(t))=a-\lambda t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\varphi}(t)=\varphi(T^{-1}(t))=a-\lambda t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The noise term satisfies
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\varphi)=bI_{1}+(a-b)I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\varphi)=bI_{1}+(a-b)I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
with</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex287" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex287.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u,\qquad I_{2}=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left(\frac{1-e^{-2uT}-2uTe^{-2uT}}{4Tu^{1+1/\beta}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u,\qquad I_{2}=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left(\frac{1-e^{-2uT}-2uTe^{-2uT}}{4Tu^{1+1/\beta}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Noticing <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a-\lambda T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a-\lambda T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda T=a-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda T=a-b</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex288"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex288.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathcal{K}(T-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T}\mathcal{K}(T-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex288.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(T-t)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{T}\left(\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2u(T-t)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\right)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex289"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex289.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2uT}\left(\int_{0}^{T}e^{2ut}(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2uT}\left(\int_{0}^{T}e^{2ut}(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex290"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex290.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2uT}\left[\frac{a}{2u}\left(e^{2uT}-1\right)-\frac{\lambda}{2u}\left(Te^{2uT}-\frac{e^{2uT}-1}{2u}\right)\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-1/\beta}e^{-2uT}\left[\frac{a}{2u}\left(e^{2uT}-1\right)-\frac{\lambda}{2u}\left(Te^{2uT}-\frac{e^{2uT}-1}{2u}\right)\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex291"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex291.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left[\frac{a}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{ae^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{\lambda T}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{\lambda(1-e^{-2uT})}{4u^{1+1/\beta}}\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left[\frac{a}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{ae^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{\lambda T}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{\lambda(1-e^{-2uT})}{4u^{1+1/\beta}}\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex292"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex292.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left[\frac{a-\lambda T}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{(a-\lambda T+\lambda T)e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{\lambda(1-e^{-2uT})}{4u^{1+1/\beta}}\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left[\frac{a-\lambda T}{2u^{1/\beta}}-\frac{(a-\lambda T+\lambda T)e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{\lambda(1-e^{-2uT})}{4u^{1+1/\beta}}\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex293"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex293.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(a-\lambda T)\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\lambda T\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left(-\frac{e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{4Tu^{1+1/\beta}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(a-\lambda T)\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u+\lambda T\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\left(-\frac{e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}+\frac{1-e^{-2uT}}{4Tu^{1+1/\beta}}\right)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next bound <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> separately.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, then <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}=\frac{\beta}{2\beta-1}+o_{T,M}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}=\frac{\beta}{2\beta-1}+o_{T,M}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex294" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex294.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{\beta(1-M^{-(\beta-1)})}{2(\beta-1)}=:A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{1}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{\beta(1-M^{-(\beta-1)})}{2(\beta-1)}=:A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex295" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex295.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{1}{2(2T)^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{T/M^{\beta}}^{T}\frac{e^{-r}}{r^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(1+\frac{1}{\beta})}{2^{2-1/\beta}}\frac{1}{T^{1-1/\beta}}=:B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}\frac{e^{-2uT}}{2u^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u=\frac{1}{2(2T)^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{T/M^{\beta}}^{T}\frac{e^{-r}}{r^{1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\leqslant\frac{\Gamma(1+\frac{1}{\beta})}{2^{2-1/\beta}}\frac{1}{T^{1-1/\beta}}=:B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we complete the proof by noting <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}=A-B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}=A-B</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.6</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex296" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex296.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}\eqsim\frac{\beta\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{4T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}\eqsim\frac{\beta\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{4T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=uT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=uT</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by a change of variable, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex297" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}=\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}\frac{1-e^{-2r}-2re^{-2r}}{r^{1+1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=:\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}q_{\beta}(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}=\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}\frac{1-e^{-2r}-2re^{-2r}}{r^{1+1/\beta}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r=:\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}q_{\beta}(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to verify that for any <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{r\geqslant 0}q_{\beta}(r)\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{r\geqslant 0}q_{\beta}(r)\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\beta}(r)\eqsim r^{-1-1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\beta}(r)\eqsim r^{-1-1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. We refer to Figure <a href="#A4.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof for The Exponential-Decay LRS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for Section ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> for an illustration of <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\beta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\beta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19189v1/qbeta.svg" id="A4.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/149;" width="191" height="149"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A4.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of the function <math id="A4.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\beta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\beta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T/M^{\beta}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T/M^{\beta}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large such that <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}q_{\beta}(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\eqsim\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}q_{\beta}(r)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r\eqsim\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and thus
we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex298" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}=\frac{\beta+o_{M,T}(1)}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}=\frac{\beta+o_{M,T}(1)}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T/M^{\beta}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T/M^{\beta}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds for all <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5\leqslant 1-e^{-2r}-2re^{-2r}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5\leqslant 1-e^{-2r}-2re^{-2r}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> . Thus, there exists a <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{T,M}\in[0.5,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{T,M}\in[0.5,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex299"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex299.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{T,M}\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}r^{-1-1/\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{T,M}\frac{1}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\int_{\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}}^{T}r^{-1-1/\beta}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex300"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex300.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{C_{T,M}\beta}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\left(\left(\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}\right)^{-1/\beta}-T^{-1/\beta}\right)=\frac{C_{T,M}\beta(M-1)}{4T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{C_{T,M}\beta}{4T^{1-1/\beta}}\left(\left(\frac{T}{M^{\beta}}\right)^{-1/\beta}-T^{-1/\beta}\right)=\frac{C_{T,M}\beta(M-1)}{4T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two cases, we complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.7</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Scaling law for exp-decay LRS). ‣ 5.2 Exponential Decay LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> in the main paper)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We consider the exponentially decaying learning rate schedule</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex301" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex301.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\tau)=ae^{-\lambda\tau},\text{ with }\varphi(K)=b," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\tau)=ae^{-\lambda\tau},\text{ with }\varphi(K)=b,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under this learning rate schedule, for the top-<math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> projection matrix
or the random projection with probability at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-\Omega(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-\Omega(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex302" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T^{1/\beta}\}}{T}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T^{1/\beta}\}}{T}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(a-b)K/\log(a/b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(a-b)K/\log(a/b)</annotation></semantics></math> is the total intrinsic training time.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the functional scaling laws (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In Theorem 4.1 (Intrinsic-time Functional Scaling Law (FSL)). ‣ 4 Functional Scaling Laws ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex303" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex303.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\mathcal{N}(\varphi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\mathcal{N}(\varphi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The noise term <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated by Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Proof for The Exponential-Decay LRS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for Section ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> and the bound on <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex304" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\varphi)=bI_{1}+(a-b)I_{2}\eqsim b+(a-b)\frac{\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\varphi)=bI_{1}+(a-b)I_{2}\eqsim b+(a-b)\frac{\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">which gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex305" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex305.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{T}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min(M,T^{1/\beta})}{T}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">so we complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.8</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a total data size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal strategy for minimizing
the final population risk when <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\frac{a}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\frac{a}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is given
by <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-\frac{s\beta}{s\beta+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-\frac{s\beta}{s\beta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(D/\log D)^{-s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}:=\frac{D}{\log K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}:=\frac{D}{\log K}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Scaling law for exp-decay LRS). ‣ 5.2 Exponential Decay LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex306" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex306.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\frac{\min(M,(\gamma\tilde{D})^{\frac{1}{\beta}})}{\tilde{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\frac{\min(M,(\gamma\tilde{D})^{\frac{1}{\beta}})}{\tilde{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\leqslant\gamma\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\leqslant\gamma\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex307" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex307.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We see that in this case <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> should be as large as possible,
since <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this case <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow><mo>≳</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality at <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above equality condition can be acheived
as <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}=\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}&lt;\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}=\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}&lt;\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we have
that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex308" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex308.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{a}{B}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{a}{B}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
which forces <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quantity <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence the optimal <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> in this case is <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which transfers to case 2.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;\gamma\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;\gamma\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex309" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex309.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly in this case <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and by AM-GM inequality,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex310" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex310.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≳</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma\tilde{D})^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with equality at <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta-1-s\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta-1-s\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality can be achieved, hence we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex311" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex311.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex312" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex312.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}^{-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, as <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\lesssim\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≲</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\lesssim\tilde{D}^{1-\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≳</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\gtrsim\tilde{D}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log K\eqsim\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log K\eqsim\log D</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the two cases together, we see that <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> can always achieves the optimal rate, hence the conclusion
follows.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.9</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a large total compute budget <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal strategy for
minimizing the final population risk—expressed in terms of the effective
maximum learning rate <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, model size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, and data size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>—is
given by:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the optimal scaling laws are:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex313" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex313.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex314" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex314.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the optimal scaling laws are</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex315" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex315.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex316" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex316.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}=D/\log K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}=D/\log K</annotation></semantics></math>. For similar reasons as in the derivation of data-optimal scaling, we may assume <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log K\eqsim\log C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log K\eqsim\log C</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify the proof. At this point, the loss can be reformulated as follows.</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex317" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex317.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{\min\{M,(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}\}}{\tilde{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{\min\{M,(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}\}}{\tilde{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&lt;\gamma\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&lt;\gamma\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex318" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex318.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> only appears in the second term, and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
monotone decreasing with <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that when <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized,
it must hold that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex319" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex319.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we
then consider a weighted AM-GM inequality, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex320" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex320.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}=\sigma^{2}\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}=\sigma^{2}\frac{M}{\tilde{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Combining with <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=MD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=MD</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex321" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex321.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex322" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex322.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
we set <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly, and proceed as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex323" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex323.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex324" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex324.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\geqslant\gamma\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\geqslant\gamma\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex325" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex325.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}}{\tilde{D}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}}{\tilde{D}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> only appears in the second term, and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically decreasing in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that when <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized, it must hold that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex326" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex326.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D})^{1/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">And then the rest is identical to the first case.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof for the WSD-Like LRS</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 5.4 (Scaling law for WSD-like LRS). ‣ 5.3 WSD-like LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>, we first present the following lemma, which gives an upper bound for the SGD noise induced by the stable phase.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.10</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex327" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex327.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\lesssim\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\lesssim\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex328"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex328.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex328.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u(T_{2}+t)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u(T_{2}+t)}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex329"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex329.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2uT_{2}}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u}{2u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{M^{-\beta}}^{1}u^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2uT_{2}}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u}{2u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex330"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex330.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{1}{T_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\int_{T_{2}M^{-\beta}}^{T_{2}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{1}{T_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\int_{T_{2}M^{-\beta}}^{T_{2}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the integral <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math> is
convergent, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex331" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex331.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\lesssim\frac{1}{T_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\lesssim\frac{1}{T_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}&gt;M^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}&gt;M^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, similarly we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex332"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex332.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex332.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim M^{1-\beta}\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u\frac{T_{2}}{M^{\beta}}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim M^{1-\beta}\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u\frac{T_{2}}{M^{\beta}}}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{T_{2}}{M^{\beta}}\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{T_{2}}{M^{\beta}}\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex333"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{M}{T_{2}}p\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2up}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\frac{M}{T_{2}}p\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2up}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex334"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex334.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{M}{T_{2}}\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim\frac{M}{T_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{M}{T_{2}}\int_{1}^{M^{\beta}}u^{-\frac{1}{\beta}}e^{-2u}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}u\eqsim\frac{M}{T_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Where the last line is because <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pe^{-2up}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pe^{-2up}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing in <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> when
<math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,p\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,p\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.11</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 5.4 (Scaling law for WSD-like LRS). ‣ 5.3 WSD-like LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> in the main paper)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the FSL (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In Theorem 4.1 (Intrinsic-time Functional Scaling Law (FSL)). ‣ 4 Functional Scaling Laws ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,K</annotation></semantics></math> are sufficiently large. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex335" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex335.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\sigma^{2}\left(\frac{b}{B}+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{1/\beta}\}}{BT_{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+T^{-s}+\sigma^{2}\left(\frac{b}{B}+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{1/\beta}\}}{BT_{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=aK_{1}+(a-b)K_{2}/\log(a/b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=aK_{1}+(a-b)K_{2}/\log(a/b)</annotation></semantics></math> is the total intrinsic training time, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}=(a-b)K_{2}/\log(a/b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}=(a-b)K_{2}/\log(a/b)</annotation></semantics></math> is the decay-phase intrinsic training time.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the results of the exponential decay LRS, let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\log(a/b)/K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\log(a/b)/K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex336" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex336.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{T(K)}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)a\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\int_{0}^{T_{2}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}-t)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{T(K)}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)a\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+\int_{0}^{T_{2}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}-t)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence by the estimation of the noise term of the exponential decay LRS (see the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 5.3 (Scaling law for exp-decay LRS). ‣ 5.2 Exponential Decay LRS ‣ 5 The Role of Learning Rate Schedules ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex337" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex337.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{T_{2}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}-t)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\eqsim b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{T_{2}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}-t)(a-\lambda t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t\eqsim b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we know</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex338"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex338.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T(K)}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{T(K)}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)\gamma_{\varphi}(t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex338.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)a\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T(K)-t)a\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex339"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex339.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim a\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim a\int_{0}^{T_{1}}\mathcal{K}(T_{2}+t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}t+b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex340"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex340.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqsim b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}.\qquad\text{(by using Lemma~\ref{lem: wsd-stable-noise})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>(by using Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma D.10. ‣ D.3 Proof for the WSD-Like LRS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for Section ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqsim b+\frac{(a-b)\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}.\qquad\text{(by using Lemma~\ref{lem: wsd-stable-noise})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the loss is given by</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex341" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex341.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim\frac{1}{T^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim\frac{1}{T^{s}}+M^{-s\beta}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{B}\left(b+(a-b)\frac{\min\{M,T_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\}}{T_{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.12</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A4.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\frac{a}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\frac{a}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have the following data-optimal strategy:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geqslant 1-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geqslant 1-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have </span><math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log D)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log D)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}},(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}},(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
and </span><math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{s\beta+1}}(\log D)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{s\beta+1}}(\log D)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A4.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;1-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;1-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have </span><math id="A4.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A4.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
and </span><math id="A4.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the total intrinsic time <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\lesssim\gamma D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\lesssim\gamma D</annotation></semantics></math>, we can always take <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\eqsim\gamma D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\eqsim\gamma D</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}:=\frac{D_{2}}{\log K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}:=\frac{D_{2}}{\log K}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem11" title="Theorem D.11 (Theorem in the main paper). ‣ D.3 Proof for the WSD-Like LRS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for Section ‣ Appendix ‣ Unveiling the Role of Learning Rate Schedules via Functional Scaling Laws" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.11</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex342" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex342.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\frac{\min(M,(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}})}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\frac{\min(M,(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}})}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\leqslant\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\leqslant\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex343" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex343.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We see that in this case <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> should be as large as possible,
since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this case <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≳</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}\gtrsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above equality condition can be achieved
as <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}=\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}&lt;\tilde{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}=\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}&lt;\tilde{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we have
that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex344" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex344.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{a}{B}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{a}{B}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
which forces <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quantity <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing with respect to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence the optimal <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> in this case is <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which transfers to case 2.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&gt;\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&gt;\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex345" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex345.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly in this case <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and by AM-GM inequality,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex346" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex346.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with equality at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality can be achieved, hence we have
that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim\frac{D}{\log K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex347" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex347.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log K)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log K)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log K)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}(\log K)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have
either <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reach the minimum risk,
in both cases we require <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{D}_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{D}_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> (this gives <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D</annotation></semantics></math>), and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex348" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex348.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty,\quad\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, as <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B\lesssim_{\log}D^{1-\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≲</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>log</mi></msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\lesssim_{\log}D^{1-\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K\gtrsim_{\log}D^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≳</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>log</mi></msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\gtrsim_{\log}D^{\frac{\beta}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log K\eqsim\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log K\eqsim\log D</annotation></semantics></math>,
which gives the desired rate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the two cases together, we see that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (case 2) always achieves the optimal rate, hence the conclusion
follows.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.13</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\frac{a}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\frac{a}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, under the compute constraint <math id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal strategy for
minimizing the final population risk—expressed in terms of the effective
maximum learning rate <math id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, model size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, and data size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>—is
given by:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="A4.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the optimal scaling laws are:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex349" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex349.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{2+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{2+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I6.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex350" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex350.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{2+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{2+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="A4.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the optimal scaling laws are:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex351" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex351.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}},(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}},(D_{1})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D,(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I6.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex352" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex352.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the total intrinsic time <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\lesssim\gamma D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\lesssim\gamma D</annotation></semantics></math>, we can always take <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\eqsim\gamma D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\eqsim\gamma D</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}:=\frac{D_{2}}{\log K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}:=\frac{D_{2}}{\log K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss can be reformulated as follows.</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex353" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex353.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{\min\{M,(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}\}}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\sigma^{2}\frac{\min\{M,(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}\}}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}&lt;\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}&lt;\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex354" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex354.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> only appears in the second term, and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
monotone decreasing with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that when <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized,
it must hold that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex355" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex355.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we
then consider a weighted AM-GM inequality, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex356" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex356.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-s\beta}=\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-s\beta}=\frac{M}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Combining with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex357" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex357.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{1+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{1+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex358" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex358.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{s-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}D^{-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{s-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}D^{-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Notice that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex359" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex359.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}D\geqslant\tilde{D}^{\frac{2+s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\Longrightarrow\mathcal{E}\gtrsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{1+s\beta}}D\geqslant\tilde{D}^{\frac{2+s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\Longrightarrow\mathcal{E}\gtrsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Note that this implies <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\frac{2+s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\gtrsim C\gtrsim D\implies\log D\eqsim\log C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>≳</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>≳</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\frac{2+s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\gtrsim C\gtrsim D\implies\log D\eqsim\log C</annotation></semantics></math>, and by similar reasons <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log K\eqsim\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log K\eqsim\log D</annotation></semantics></math> (the max learning rate <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\gamma\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\gamma\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Hence when <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimized, we have <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim D/\log C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim D/\log C</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex360" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex360.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{1+\beta(s-1)}{2+s\beta}},\quad M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim(C/\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},\quad D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex361" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex361.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}(C)\eqsim(C/\log C)^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
we set <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly, and proceed as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex362" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex362.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex363" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex363.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D^{-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Notice that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex364" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex364.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}D\gtrsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1+\beta}{\beta}}\Longrightarrow\mathcal{E}\gtrsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>≳</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\eqsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}D\gtrsim\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{1+\beta}{\beta}}\Longrightarrow\mathcal{E}\gtrsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Hence when <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimized, we have <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim D/\log C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{2}\eqsim D/\log C</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex365" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex365.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex366" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex366.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\beta}\geqslant\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\beta}\geqslant\gamma\tilde{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex367" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex367.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\frac{(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}}{\tilde{D}_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+\frac{1}{(\gamma D)^{s}}+\frac{(\gamma\tilde{D}_{2})^{\frac{1}{\beta}}}{\tilde{D}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By AM-GM inequality,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex368" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex368.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma D)^{-s}+\gamma^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\frac{1}{\tilde{D}_{2}^{1-\frac{1}{\beta}}}\gtrsim D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with equality at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the equality can be achieved, hence <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss can be written as follows.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex369" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex369.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+D^{-\frac{s}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{-\frac{s\beta-s}{1+s\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Combining with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=MD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=MD</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the optimal scaling laws as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex370" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex370.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{-\frac{1-1/\beta}{2+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1-1/\beta}{2+s\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{1+s\beta-\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{-\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}},M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{-\frac{1-1/\beta}{2+s\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1+s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{1-1/\beta}{2+s\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex371" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex371.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{2+s\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{2+s\beta}}(\log C)^{\frac{s\beta-s}{2+s\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leqslant 1-\frac{1}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have
either <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim 1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\eqsim D^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+s\beta}}\tilde{D}_{2}^{\frac{\beta-1}{1+s\beta}}\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reach the minimum risk,
in both cases we require <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{D}_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{D}_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> (this gives <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{2})_{\mathrm{opt}}\gtrsim D^{\frac{s\beta}{\beta-1}}\log D</annotation></semantics></math>), and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex372" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex372.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+D^{-s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,\quad\mathcal{E}_{K}\eqsim M^{-s\beta}+D^{-s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Combining with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=MD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=MD</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the optimal scaling laws as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex373" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex373.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim 1,M_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{1}{1+\beta}},D_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{\frac{\beta}{1+\beta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which leads to the following optimal final population risk:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex374" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex374.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≂</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{opt}}\eqsim C^{-\frac{s\beta}{1+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the results of each case, we get the desired optimal scaling strategy stated in the theorem.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Auxiliary Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a semi-positive definite (SPD) matrix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and
a random gaussian vector <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{H})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex375" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex375.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}\preceq\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\right]=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq 2\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}\preceq\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}-\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\right]=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq 2\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=(A_{ij})_{i,j=1,...,M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=(A_{ij})_{i,j=1,...,M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry of <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex376" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex376.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex377" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex377.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}\right]=2\mathbb{E}\left[A_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{2}\mathbf{x}_{j}^{2}\right]=2A_{ij}\lambda_{i}\lambda_{j}=2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}(i,j)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}\right]=2\mathbb{E}\left[A_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{2}\mathbf{x}_{j}^{2}\right]=2A_{ij}\lambda_{i}\lambda_{j}=2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}(i,j).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex378" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex378.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{M}A_{kk}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{2}\mathbf{x}_{k}^{2}\right]=\sum_{k\neq i}A_{kk}\lambda_{i}\lambda_{k}+3A_{ii}\lambda_{i}^{2}=2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}(i,i)+\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k,l}\mathbf{x}_{i}\mathbf{x}_{k}A_{kl}\mathbf{x}_{l}\mathbf{x}_{j}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{M}A_{kk}\mathbf{x}_{i}^{2}\mathbf{x}_{k}^{2}\right]=\sum_{k\neq i}A_{kk}\lambda_{i}\lambda_{k}+3A_{ii}\lambda_{i}^{2}=2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}(i,i)+\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the trace inequality we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex379" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex379.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\preceq\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\preceq\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> at both sides,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex380" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex380.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the results, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex381" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex381.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}]=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq 2\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐇</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐇𝐀𝐇</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}]=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+2\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}\preceq 2\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A})\mathbf{H}+\mathbf{H}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\preceq\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\preceq\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> be two positive semi-definite
(p.s.d.) matrices. Then for any p.s.d. matrix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex382" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex382.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{P}})\leqslant\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Q}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{Q}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>𝐏</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>𝐏</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>𝐐</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>𝐐</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{P}})\leqslant\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Q}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{Q}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is clear that <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{P}})=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>𝐏</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>𝐏</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔𝐏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\sqrt{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{U}\sqrt{\mathbf{P}})=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{P})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex383" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex383.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{Q})-\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{P})=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{P}))\geqslant 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔𝐏</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{Q})-\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}\mathbf{P})=\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{P}))\geqslant 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> are both SPD matrices.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
